  "standard": "TRIG.GRAPH.2",
  "difficulty": 3,
  "prompt": "What is the phase shift of $y = \\sin\\left(2x - \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$?",
  "answerType": "multiple-choice",
  "choices": [
    {
      "id": "A",
      "label": "$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ to the right",
      "correct": true
    },
    {
      "id": "B",
      "label": "$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ to the right",
      "correct": false
    },
    {
      "id": "C",
      "label": "$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ to the left",
      "correct": false
    },
    {
      "id": "D",
      "label": "$\\pi$ to the right",
      "correct": false
    }
  ],
  "primaryAnswer": "A",
  "alternativeAnswers": [],
  "acceptanceMode": "exact",
  "hint": "You cannot read the shift straight off until the $x$ inside has a coefficient of $1$.",
  "hints": [
    {
      "level": "nudge",
      "text": "You cannot read the shift straight off until the $x$ inside has a coefficient of $1$."
    },
    {
      "level": "nudge",
      "title": "🪜 Try a simpler one",
      "text": "Warm up with $y = \\sin\\left(x - \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$: the $x$ already has coefficient $1$, so you read the shift straight off as $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ right. A $2$ in front must be factored out first, which halves that shift."
    },
    {
      "level": "guide",
      "text": "Factor the $2$ out of the parentheses: $2x - \\frac{\\pi}{2} = 2\\left(x - \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$."
    },
    {
      "level": "reveal",
      "text": "Now it reads as a shift right of $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$."
    }
  ],
  "explanation": [
    "Rewrite the inside in the form $B(x - C)$: $2x - \\frac{\\pi}{2} = 2\\left(x - \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$.",
    "In $y = \\sin(B(x - C))$ the phase shift is $C$, here $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$, and the minus sign sends it right.",
    "So the graph of $\\sin(2x)$ slides $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ to the right."
  ],
  "alternativeExplanations": [
    {
      "title": "Find where the cycle starts",
      "steps": [
        "A sine cycle begins when its input is $0$: set $2x - \\frac{\\pi}{2} = 0$.",
        "Solve: $2x = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$, so $x = \\frac{\\pi}{4}$.",
        "The cycle that normally starts at $x = 0$ now starts at $x = \\frac{\\pi}{4}$ — a shift right of $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "⚠️ The trap here",
      "steps": [
        "The trap is answering $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ to the right (choice B) by reading the number off the end of the expression.",
        "That only works when the coefficient of $x$ is $1$. Here the $2$ compresses everything, so the actual slide is half as big.",
        "Rule: always factor out $B$ first, or solve \"inside $= 0$\". Both give $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$, never $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    "phase-shift",
    "factoring",
    "common-error"
  ],
